# Local-only operational watchers. These read THIS host's registry, mailbox and
# filesystem layout, so they are written to work here, not to be published. The
# auto-sync commits with `git add -A`, which stages anything not ignored -- that
# is the mechanism that published a host filesystem root, a profile name and an
# operator mailbox on 2026-09-26, and again on 2026-09-27. Published watchers
# are the genericised ones under scripts/; these stay on the host.
scripts/finch_kdp_watch.py
scripts/tseg_watch.py
scripts/test_block_ledger_hook.sh
# Same class, same reason. These were NOT listed when the 8 of them were moved
# out of the tree on 2026-09-28 (see 0c83f0f) -- an incomplete list, not a
# deliberate removal: each is the named authority of an open task, so deleting
# one makes that task's re_verify_trigger unreachable. Listed exhaustively and
# by PATTERN, because a per-file list has now failed twice: the first 3 by
# omission, and a PII gate that reports 28 findings is the only reliable
# enumerator of what must not ship.
scripts/chronicle_lock_storm_watch.py
scripts/test_chronicle_lock_storm_watch.py
scripts/finch_blocked_config_watch.py
scripts/finch_journal_write.py
scripts/test_finch_journal_write.py
scripts/finch_onemed_0929_watch.py
scripts/test_finch_onemed_0929_watch.py
scripts/finch_tokyo_ada_watch.py
# Catch-all for this class: anything reading THIS host's registry, mailbox or
# filesystem layout. Prefer a new host-only watcher being ignored by default over
# it needing a line here, so the failure is silent until the PII gate catches it.
scripts/*_watch.py
scripts/test_*_watch*.py
